WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.739 --> 00:00:07.304
When you make a plan for the day, what gets a place on the list?

2
00:00:07.304 --> 00:00:10.522
Work. Errands. Messages. Things other people need.

3
00:00:10.522 --> 00:00:15.670
Rest and connection can end up waiting until everything else is finished.

4
00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:19.019
On a busy day, that moment may never arrive.

5
00:00:19.384 --> 00:00:24.609
Consider making a little room for them in the plan you already have.

6
00:00:24.609 --> 00:00:30.236
Alongside one necessary task, you could include a brief pause and a way to

7
00:00:30.236 --> 00:00:30.637
connect.

8
00:00:31.003 --> 00:00:35.823
That might mean sitting quietly after an appointment, sending a message to

9
00:00:35.823 --> 00:00:40.243
someone you trust, or asking a friend for a short check-in.

10
00:00:40.243 --> 00:00:45.063
Connection doesn’t have to mean a large gathering or a long conversation.

11
00:00:45.063 --> 00:00:47.876
Choose people and settings that feel supportive.

12
00:00:48.241 --> 00:00:53.271
Rest can also take different forms. Think about what feels restorative to you,

13
00:00:53.271 --> 00:00:55.980
within the time and circumstances you have.

14
00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:01.095
This is a flexible idea, rather than another checklist to complete perfectly.

15
00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:06.957
If you’re isolated or carrying more than you can manage, support might come

16
00:01:06.957 --> 00:01:11.608
from a trusted person, a community resource, or a qualified professional.

17
00:01:11.608 --> 00:01:16.323
Look at your next day. Where could a little rest or connection belong?
